ADDR2LINE(1)                User Commands                ADDR2LINE(1)

NAME
    addr2line - convert addresses into file names and line numbers

SYNOPSIS
    addr2line [-afhijps] [-e file] [-j section] [address...]

DESCRIPTION
    addr2line translates addresses of an ELF64 file into the source file
    name, the line number and optionally the function name. addr2line reads the
    DWARF debug information of versions 2, 3, 4 and 5. The addresses are
    hexadecimal numbers with or without the prefix 0x. Without address
    arguments, addr2line reads one address from each line of standard
    input.

    A function that the debug information does not describe receives the
    name of the nearest symbol of the symbol table. An address that no
    section contains gives ?? and ??:0. A line number of 0 prints as ?.
    The output matches the output of the GNU addr2line.

    Compressed debug sections are not supported. addr2line reports them
    and uses the symbol table only.

OPTIONS
    -a, --addresses
        Print the address in hexadecimal before the result.
    -e file, --exe=file
        Read the debug information from file. The default is a.out.
    -f, --functions
        Print the function name before the file name and the line.
    -i, --inlines
        Print the chain of inlined calls. Each line after the first
        gives the caller of the previous line.
    -j section, --section=section
        Read the addresses as offsets in section.
    -p, --pretty-print
        Print each result on one line. Inlined callers follow on lines
        that start with (inlined by).
    -s, --basenames
        Print file names without the directory.
    -h, --help
        Print the usage and exit.

EXAMPLES
    addr2line -fip -e a.out 0x401136
    echo 0x401136 | addr2line -e a.out

SEE ALSO
    nm(1), objdump(1), readelf(1)
